      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242782",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/1d/1d2fd224dc3f59bec5f335e90a4a7b2da0cdb83f809283f06d6dc3954a27815c.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $ABCD$ is a parallelogram, and $\u2220A$ is a right angle.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$ABCD$ is a rectangle.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $ABCD$ is a parallelogram | Given |\n| 2 | $\u2220A$ is a right angle | Given |\n| 3 | $m\u2220A = 90^{\u2218}$ | Definition of a right angle |\n| 4 | $\u2220C\u2245\u2220A$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 5 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 6 | $m\u2220A + m\u2220D = 180^{\u2218}$ | Definition of supplementary angles |\n| 7 | $90^{\u2218} + m\u2220D = 180^{\u2218}$ | Substitution |\n| 8 | $m\u2220D = 90^{\u2218}$ | Algebra |\n| 9 | $\u2220D$ is a right angle | Definition of a right angle |\n| 10 | $\u2220B\u2245\u2220D$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 11 | $\u2220B$ and $\u2220C$ are right angles | All right angles are congruent |\n| 12 | $ABCD$ is a rectangle | Definition of a rectangle |"
    },
