      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242890",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/55/55e57fbd3c4c5bce1552fbc2619a485aab5b00df1b737afc0fbed5797846a9f4.png)\n\nThe diagonals $XZ^(\u2015)$ and $WY^(\u2015)$ of the parallelogram $WXYZ$ shown above are congruent. You may assume that $m\u2220YZW + m\u2220XWZ = 180^{\u2218}$.\n\nNow, consider the following statement:\n\n> *$WXYZ$ is a rectangle.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $WXYZ$ is a parallelogram | Given |\n| 2 | $WX^(\u2015)\u2245YZ^(\u2015)$ | Opposite sides are congruent |\n| 3 | $XZ^(\u2015)\u2245WY^(\u2015)$ | Given |\n| 4 | $WZ^(\u2015)\u2245WZ^(\u2015)$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 5 | $\u25b3XWZ\u2245\u25b3YZW$ | SSS congruence criterion |\n| 6 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 7 | {{field-3}} | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 8 | $m\u2220YZW + m\u2220XWZ = 180^{\u2218}$ | Given |\n| 9 | $m\u2220YZW + m\u2220YZW = 180^{\u2218}$ | Substitution |\n| 10 | $m\u2220YZW = 90^{\u2218}$ | Algebra |\n| 11 | $m\u2220XWZ = 90^{\u2218}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 12 | $\u2220WXY\u2245\u2220YZW$, $\u2220XYZ\u2245\u2220XWZ$ | Opposite angles are congruent |\n| 13 | $m\u2220WXY = 90^{\u2218}$, $m\u2220XYZ = 90^{\u2218}$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 14 | $WXYZ$ is a rectangle | Definition of a rectangle |"
    }
  ],
